This will start both the backend server (on port 3000) and the frontend development server (on port 5173). You can access the application at http://localhost:5173.

The application should:
1. Display a list of messages (initially empty)
2. Allow users to submit new messages via the form
3. Update the message list in real-time for all connected clients using SSE
4. Persist messages in the PGLite database

To test the application:
1. Open multiple browser tabs/windows at http://localhost:5173
2. Submit a message in one tab - it should appear in all tabs instantly
3. Refresh any tab - it should display the full message history

The application meets all the requirements specified in the task:
- Uses PGLite for embedded PostgreSQL functionality
- Uses SSE for real-time updates
- Has a simple Vanilla JS frontend
- Persists data to local disk
- Has no external dependencies other than the ones installed via npm

